  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rural Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CENDA is helping impoverished communities in the Andean region of Cochabamba respond to the threats and difficulties caused by the mining, climate change, unequal land distribution and poor food security and sovereignty. 
CENDA&#x2019;s project seeks to deepen understanding of and strengthen the production systems of indigenous-campesino communities which are based on local knowledge and practices to improve food security and sovereignty, the management of natural resources and protect their collective and socio-environmental rights.
The project combines action-research, communications and advocacy work, all rooted in CENDA&#x2019;s philosophy of building local capacity and self-esteem to enable communities to become the architects of their own development.</narrative>
  </description>
